---
description: Modernization vs. new-construction classification guide
alwaysApply: true
---

Modernization tender structural signature: three linked spec sections, commonly numbered 14000 (general/bid instructions), 14100 (general technical modernization spec), and 14900 (a per-car/per-building schedule with existing-equipment make/model). Some consultants combine these into a single section number (e.g. ATTA's "14200") but keep the same three-part internal structure — look for the shape (bid instructions + general spec + per-unit schedule), not the literal section number. Direct parts emails requesting specific replacement parts are also qualify-favoring modernization/parts orders.

New-construction tender structural signature: a single consultant-authored specification (no split general/schedule sections) covering literally every elevator subsystem from scratch — commonly structured as PART 1 - GENERAL / PART 2 - PRODUCTS / PART 3 - EXECUTION for a brand new building. If you see this shape, classify as new_construction and default toward disqualify per the policy above.
